  - continual learning
  - machine unlearning
  - knowledge conflicts
abstract: >-
  A unified framework organizing LLM knowledge management into five structural
  stages (Acquisition, Storage, Retrieval, Update, Forgetting), with two
  technical contributions: the Provenance Vector, an architectural proposal that
  gates stale parametric activations using acquisition metadata, and Lifecycle
  Desynchronization, a KL-based metric quantifying the failure that occurs when
  parametric weights and retrieved context conflict, measured reproducibly on
  GPT-2.
